    "title": "Santa Barbara Residents Alerted to Scam Emails Posing as City Payment Requests - NewsBreak",
    "text": "37 minutes ago The City of Santa Barbara has warned residents about scam emails that pretend to be from City departments and request payments. These emails may use City logos and formal language but are not official. City officials state that the City does not ask for wire transfers or unusual payment methods.\nResidents should use only the official Accela Citizen Access (ACA) platform for payments. The City advises people to watch for urgent payment requests, requests for sensitive information, unusual language, and emails from unknown senders. These are common signs of scams.\nIf you receive a suspicious invoice or message claiming to be from the City, do not respond or send money. Contact the City directly using verified contact information. Sharing this information can help others avoid scams.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
